<title>SINGAPORE: PCI plunges to 1995/96 net loss.</title>
<headline>PCI plunges to 1995/96 net loss.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss				 21.94 vs   3.60 (profit)</p>
<p>    Net loss per share (cents)	 12.7  vs   2.1  (profit)</p>
<p>    Turnover				127.33 vs 245.19</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	 3.51 vs   5.15</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		    1.25 vs   2.19</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation	   7.95 vs   7.70</p>
<p>    Pre-tax loss			   23.53 vs   2.77 (profit)</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	     0.48 vs   2.90</p>
<p>    Tax				(gain) 1.09 vs   2.04 (loss)</p>
<p>    Minorities		     (gain) 0.02 vs   0.04 (loss)</p>
<p>Note - PCI Ltd makes and sells printed circuit boards, liquid crystal displays, modules and cordless telephones.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
